%% Server-side ingestion — sequence diagram (temporal view)
%% Render: https://mermaid.live  or any Mermaid-aware Markdown viewer
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User / Browser
    participant API as Next.js API (Vercel)
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant B as AWS Batch
    participant W as Fargate Worker
    participant DB as Supabase Postgres
    participant RT as Supabase Realtime
    participant SES as AWS SES

    Note over U: Extract columns (CSV header / Parquet footer) + confirm mapping

    U->>API: POST /api/ingest/initiate (metadata, file list)
    API->>DB: create Dataset=UPLOADING + UploadSession + UploadFile[]
    API-->>U: presigned upload URLs

    rect rgb(240, 247, 255)
    Note over U,S3: Upload phase — full-screen overlay, close guards active
    loop each raw file (multipart if >100 MB)
        U->>S3: direct upload to raw/{id}/  (bytes bypass Vercel)
        Note over U: overlay updates MB/MB + ETA
        U->>API: POST files/{key}/complete
    end
    end

    U->>API: POST /api/ingest/{id}/complete
    API->>DB: status = QUEUED
    API->>B: SubmitJob (tier-sized vCPU/RAM)
    API-->>U: uploaded — safe to close tab / navigate

    B->>W: run container
    W->>API: callback status=PROCESSING
    API->>DB: status=PROCESSING
    W->>S3: download raw/{id}/
    W->>W: run process_*.py

    rect rgb(255, 247, 230)
    Note over W,RT: Live processing progress (GitHub-Actions style)
    loop each stage
        W->>API: callback progress (stage, %)
        API->>DB: write processingProgress
        DB->>RT: row change
        RT-->>U: live update (dashboard)
    end
    end

    W->>S3: upload datasets/{id}/ (chunked output)
    W->>S3: delete raw/{id}/
    W->>API: callback status=COMPLETE (stats, fingerprint)
    API->>DB: status=COMPLETE, completedAt
    API->>SES: send email
    SES-->>U: "Your dataset is ready" + viewer link
